# WIFI

On Raspberry Pi OS with NetworkManager, first list saved connection names:

```bash
nmcli connection show
```

Then disconnect the old network and connect to a saved one:

```bash
sudo nmcli connection down id "Old WiFi" && sudo nmcli connection up id "New WiFi"

sudo nmcli connection down id "Arduino-Hotspot" && sudo nmcli connection up id "Vodafone-FC2C"

sudo nmcli connection down id "Vodafone-FC2C" && sudo nmcli connection up id "Arduino-Hotspot"

```



If the new network isn’t saved yet:

```bash
sudo nmcli connection down id "Old WiFi" && sudo nmcli device wifi connect "New SSID" password "PASSWORD" ifname wlan0
```

If you’re connected over SSH through the old Wi-Fi, the session will drop when it disconnects.


